  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (an untitled health and wellness program, Health Care Administration, and a partially cut-off Homeland Security and Emergency Management program). The ledger was built for the Bachelor of Arts in Health Care Administration because it is the only one fully captured. Please confirm this is the intended program.",
    "The capture does not explicitly label the credit unit as semester credits. 'semester' is assumed.",
    "The capture says Global Campus Foundations courses 'may be substituted'. The 11 courses listed are the standard sequence (33 credits), not a fixed list.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled first and satisfies 3 elective credits. GEN 104 also counts toward electives for students transferring fewer than 30 credits. The capture does not say whether these are mandatory parts of the 51 elective credits.",
    "The residency requirement is a minimum of 30 credits completed at the University. The capture does not tie it to specific courses, so no requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Upper-division requirements are a minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 in the major. The capture does not map these to specific elective choices.",
    "ACC 281 requires the Quantitative Reasoning requirement to be met first. The capture does not state which Foundations course satisfies Quantitative Reasoning.",
    "HCA 305 appears as an alternative prerequisite but is not described in the capture."
  ],
